<h3>A paradigm shift</h3>
<p>The focus in working with AI has kept moving.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Prompt engineering</strong> &mdash; how to talk with the AI (how to ask).</li>
    <li><strong>Context engineering</strong> &mdash; what knowledge · data to give along with it.</li>
    <li><strong>Harness engineering</strong> &mdash; how to compose not a single model but <strong>the entire environment surrounding the model</strong>.</li>
</ul>

<h3>"Hand the steering wheel to the AI"</h3>
<p>In the existing way, <strong>the human always held the steering wheel</strong> and the AI only assisted from the side. So there was productivity only while the human was holding the wheel. The harness is an approach that <strong>hands that steering wheel to the AI</strong> so it performs many tasks at the same time, autonomously, for a long time.</p>

<div class="note">
    <span class="nh">The word 'harness'</span>
    Harness comes from the <strong>tack of a horse-drawn carriage</strong>. It is a metaphor that how well you equip yourself to drive the horse (the AI) determines performance. It works both for a single agent and for a multi configuration that binds several agents together.
</div>
